    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nInterested in this property? Sign up for mySherryFitz to arrange your viewing, see current offers or make your own offer. Register now at SherryFitz.ie.\n\nA rare opportunity to acquire a fully renovated, double-fronted red-brick period residence in a superb central location.\n\nOccupying a commanding position at the beginning of prestigious Rectory Road, Elderwood is an impressive five-bedroom detached home, less than five minutes' walk from Enniscorthy town centre. Beautifully renewed while retaining its distinctive architectural character, the property is presented in walk-in condition, ready for its first occupants following comprehensive renovation.\n\nThe improvements extend well beyond decoration. A newly fitted kitchen with Neff appliances, entirely new bathrooms, new plumbing throughout and a new oil-fired central heating system with a high-efficiency condensing oil boiler bring modern comfort to this characterful home. High levels of insulation throughout, a fully insulated attic and double-glazed windows throughout further complement the extensive works.\n\nJust as importantly, the renovation has preserved the details that give Elderwood its individuality. The attractive marble fireplace, distinctive curved archway upstairs and handsome red-brick frontage sit comfortably alongside bright, neutral interiors and warm-toned flooring.\n\nGround-Floor Accommodation\nA welcoming entrance hall leads to the principal living spaces. The separate front sitting room is centred around an attractive marble fireplace and enjoys generous natural light, offering a comfortable retreat with an enduring sense of character.\nAt the heart of the home is the newly fitted kitchen and dining area, featuring extensive cabinetry, quartz worktops, a substantial central island and Neff appliances. Together with the adjoining family space, it provides a welcoming setting for everyday meals, relaxed evenings and entertaining. The separate sitting room adds the flexibility of a second, distinct reception space.\nA newly fitted ground-floor WC completes the downstairs accommodation.\n\nBedrooms & Bathrooms\nThe five-bedroom accommodation offers flexibility for family living, visiting guests or a dedicated home office.\nThe principal suite is a particular highlight, combining the bedroom with its own walk-in wardrobe room, extensive fitted storage and an entirely new ensuite shower room.\nThe newly fitted family bathroom includes both a bath and a separate shower. A bright landing and the retained curved archway add further character to the upper floor.\n\nOutside Space\nTo the rear, a patio area provides an ideal setting for alfresco dining, morning coffee or relaxed outdoor entertaining.\nThe property also benefits from very private rear parking for three cars, a particularly valuable feature in such a central location. Pleasant elevated views across Enniscorthy add to the appeal of its setting.\n\nLocation\nElderwood combines an established residential address with the convenience of having the town close at hand. Enniscorthy town centre is less than five minutes' walk away, with cafés, shops and everyday services within easy reach.\nThe locality offers an excellent choice of primary and secondary schools, together with a wide range of shops and supermarkets. Convenient access to the M11 motorway provides easy onward travel to Dublin and Dublin Airport.\nHigh-speed fibre broadband is available at the property, supporting home working and modern family life.\nFor buyers seeking a distinctive detached home without taking on a renovation project, Elderwood brings together character, comfort and convenience in one compelling package."
      },
