        "Content": "<ul><li>Fully renovated, five-bedroom, double-fronted red-brick detached period residence</li><li>Generous accommodation extending to approximately 140 sq. m. (1,507 sq. ft.)</li><li>Commanding position at the beginning of prestigious Rectory Road, less than five minutes' walk from the town centre</li><li>Walk-in condition, ready for its first occupants following comprehensive renovation</li><li>Newly fitted kitchen with Neff appliances, quartz worktops and a substantial central island</li><li>Adjoining family space and separate front sitting room with marble fireplace</li><li>Principal suite with walk-in wardrobe room, extensive fitted storage and new ensuite</li><li>Entirely new bathrooms, including a family bathroom with bath and separate shower, plus a ground-floor WC</li><li>New plumbing throughout and new oil-fired central heating system with a high-efficiency condensing oil boiler</li><li>High levels of insulation throughout, fully insulated attic and double-glazed windows throughout</li><li>Retained architectural character, including the distinctive curved upstairs archway</li><li>Rear patio ideal for alfresco dining, very private parking for three cars and elevated town views</li><li>Excellent choice of local schools, shops and supermarkets, with convenient M11 access for Dublin and Dublin Airport</ul>"
